{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "chain-so2-co2e-mechanism-control-runspec",
    "description": "The `chain-so2-co2e-mechanism-control` RunSpec: 22 pollutant-processes over 22 pollutants, 2,309 rows. Reproduced from the DEFAULT database.\n\nWHAT IT IS. It is the control twin of `chain-so2-co2e-mechanism`, and it differs from it in exactly one selection: five pollutants are NOT selected -- SO2 (31), NonHAPTOG (88), Atmospheric CO2 (90), CO2 Equivalent (98) and the NonHAPTOG Mechanism pseudo-pollutant (3000). Same county, year, month, day, hour, source type, road type and the same four fuel types. MOVES's own two answers agree to the BIT on all 2,309 shared rows, so nothing here is new arithmetic: what this document tests is GATING, and every way it can fail is this port emitting something the RunSpec did not ask for or dropping something it did.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. Three of the five deselected pollutants are the three whose machinery does NOT come from the run's own tables, which is why the twin is worth a document at all.\n(1) A DECLARED EDGE LIST MUST STILL BE SELECTION-GATED. `CO2AERunningStartExtendedIdleCalculator`'s four chain edges are declared in the model, not read from `runspecchainedto`, because `pollutantprocessassoc.chainedTo1/2` are NULL on 9001 and 9801 (conventions 77). A declared edge is present in every run. Here 9001 and 9801 are not selected, so no rate row carries them and the sixteen edge-process pairs must all stay silent -- against a sibling where they produce 250 rows.\n(2) THE MECHANISM SWITCH FROM THE OTHER SIDE. NonHAPTOG is switched on by the mechanism pseudo-pollutant and not by selecting 88 (conventions 78). `chain-nonhaptog` selects 88 with no mechanism; this run selects NEITHER, and the leaf must be off from both sides at once.\n(3) ONE FEWER ROW IN `runspecchainedto`. 20 edges here against the sibling's 21: the missing one is SO2's 3101 off Total Energy's 9101. The chain's edge relation is the run's table unioned with the declared list, so dropping one table row must drop exactly one pollutant's block and leave the other twenty-one untouched.\n(4) AN ENERGY ROOT WITH NO CHILDREN. 9101 Total Energy is still selected and still the widest block at 125 cohorts, and it is the only run in this corpus where nothing is chained off it. The kilojoule divisor the edge weight carries (conventions 77) therefore has to be invisible here, where in the sibling it is a factor of 1,055,055.9 on two pollutants.\n(5) THE REST UNMOVED. The hydrocarbon ladder, TOG's fan-in, the fourteen toxics off VOC and ethanol's narrow 64-cohort block -- narrow because ethanol's ratio covers only the two gasoline fuels, 1 and 5 -- are all still here, and all of them must be unchanged to the digit.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "chain-so2-co2e-mechanism-control",
      "control",
      "gating",
      "hc-speciation",
      "chained",
      "ragged",
      "air-toxics",
      "calculator-edges"
    ]
  },
